es and Data Schemas"), ": Define domain entities using dataclasses and type annotations, locking down field structures and value constraints."), "\n", React.createElement(_components.li, null, React.createElement(_components.strong, null, "Declare Explicit Method Signatures and Type Bounds"), ": Write complete function signatures, parameter type hints, and return types for all public module APIs. Write detailed docstrings defining system invariants and boundary conditions."), "\n", React.createElement(_components.li, null, React.createElement(_components.strong, null, "Insert Execution Placeholders (", React.createElement(_components.code, null, "pass"), " and ", React.createElement(_components.code, null, "..."), ")"), ": Place ", React.createElement(_components.code, null, "pass"), " or Ellipsis (", React.createElement(_components.code, null, "..."), ") inside function bodies. This explicitly signals to the agent that execution logic is required while locking down surrounding interface structures."), "\n", React.createElement(_components.li, null, React.createElement(_components.strong, null, "Execute Polyglot Generation with Context Lockdown"), ": Direct the AI agent to consume the Python schema and implement or refactor the primary production files (e.g., Rust services) against the schema definition."), "\n"), "\n", React.createElement(_components.h3, null, "2.3 Risk-Driven Software Architecture"), "\n", React.createElement(_components.p, null, "Modern AI-assisted development adapts George Fairbanks' risk-driven architectural methodology (", React.createElement(_components.em, null, "Just Enough Software Architecture"), "). Architectural effort should not be uniformly applied; design investment must scale proportionally to the operational, safety, and financial risks of the target component."), "\n", React.createElement(_components.p, null, "Fairbanks illustrates this concept through the analogy of a civil engineer installing a mailbox: the engineer does not per